 "notes": "DAMNED experiment (Savalle et al., Paris Observatory). Digitised the green 'DAMNED' curve from the top-left panel of Fig. 3: 95% CL upper limit on d_e in the standard galactic DM halo model (rho_DM = 0.4 GeV/cm^3), assuming only d_e nonzero ('maximum reach' approach, d_me set to zero). Mass range 4.1e-11 to 8.3e-10 eV (10-200 kHz). Axis calibration from figure gridlines/ticks (log-log); per-column log-midpoint of the curve, with the extremes of the narrow resonance dips/peaks (cavity mechanical resonances at 27.6, 82.8, 138, 193 kHz) added explicitly; deepest dip reaches d_e ~ 9e-2 at 1.14e-10 eV. Paper also constrains d_me (top-right panel, same procedure) and gives much stronger constraints in an Earth relaxion-halo overdensity scenario (bottom panels); the standard galactic-DM d_e curve is reported here. Narrow frequency bands in Tab. I are excluded due to systematics. Paper notes resonance-peak frequency/amplitude uncertain at ~5% level.",
